[title "WK neo riemannian"]

\key c \major \numericTimeSignature \time 4/4 \clef "treble" <bf df f>1^\markup "Neo-Riemannian transformations relate one major and one minor triad. \n• Every transformation toggles back and forth between the same two triads. \n• Example 3 in the Neo-Riemannian chapter concisely summarizes Parallel (P), Relative (R), and \n    Leading-tone exchange (L).\n• Example 13 in the chapter summarizes Slide, Nebenverwandt (N), and Hexatonic pole (H)."^\markup "You are given a starting chord, and below the staff, a transformation.\n• Apply the requested Neo-Riemannian transformation, and notate the chord in the empty measure.\n• Write the appropriate chord symbol above each chord.\nThe first exercise has been completed as an example."^\markup "1" \chords "Bbmi" \addlyrics { P } | %1

